{"actor":"dashboard:web","data":{"description":"We have buildings across the country, each equipped with a small sensor device that monitors temperature, and humidity. These devices periodically send us readings via an HTTP integration.\nWe need a way to automatically flag when something seems wrong. For example:\n\u2022  If a device hasn\u2019t been heard from in a while, we want to know.\n\u2022  If the conditions it\u2019s reporting seem out of the normal range, we want to know\n\u2022  If a device seems to be reporting less frequently than it should, we also want to know. \nBuild something that takes in a device\u2019s recent activity and tells us which of these problems, if any, are occurring. We should be able to configure what \u201cnormal\u201d looks like.\n\nOur app should provide an easy way to look for devices with specific failures, and check the status of each device. \n\n\nSample Payload\n\n{\n\"fCnt\": 100,\n\"devEUI\": \"abcdabcdabcdabcd\",\n\"data\": \"AQ==\",\n\"object\":{\"temperature\": 50.5 ,\"humidity\": 75.0},\n \"rxInfo\": [\n{\"gatewayID\": \"1234123412341234\",\n\"name\": \"G1\",\"time\": \"2022-07-19T11:00:00\",\n\"rssi\": -57,\"loRaSNR\": 10}\n],\n   \"txInfo\": {\"frequency\": 86810000,\"dr\": 5}\n}","priority":"medium","short_id":"HDT-10","status":"backlog","title":"Expanded functionality","type":"task"},"id":"ev_01KYT7KSQA7RMQ67VBQQPTRTT8","schema_version":1,"task_id":"task_01KYT7KSQ651ETFEDH5J2RTGRM","ts":"2026-07-30T19:21:55Z","type":"task_created"}
